  "reading": "The scripted floor detects 14 of 25 -- exactly the items whose target is No, credited to the adapter's own always_escalate policy because 'I cannot determine the answer.' contains 'no' inside 'cannot'. The synthesis Challenger on claude-cli reaches 24 of 25, eleven beyond the floor, and the policies it proposes are \"Yes No\", \"Yes/No\" and their newline variants -- the both-labels-at-once class that README.md records a human finding by hand and the declared repertoire structurally cannot express. qwen3:8b reaches 0 with the verifier and 2 without, so this is a capability threshold and not a property of the design.",
  "honesty": "One run per arm, not three: each claude-cli run is ~16 minutes. The number to distrust accordingly is the exact 24, not the direction. self_report records what the model claimed and it is used for nothing -- every detection here was scored by the deterministic exploit_gap machinery, and the model's claims disagreed with it zero times."
